  "details": "One serious issue with main-thread heavy processes is that heavy mathematical calculations sitting on that thread can seriously slow down the runtime.\nUdon especially has this problem due to the high CPU load of even individual mathematical operations compared to native Unity C#.\nA proposal to help with this would be to draw on the Node developers' solution to this same problem. Node, like normal JS, is based on a single thread that is designed to interact with the DOM. However, the Node developers recognized that a worker thread system would allow them to pull heavy mathematics jobs onto different threads.\nThis model seems like it would be interesting to explore with Udon. Some reading is below:\nhttps://nodejs.org/api/worker_threads.html\nhttps://livecodestream.dev/post/how-to-work-with-worker-threads-in-nodejs/\nhttps://nodesource.com/blog/worker-threads-nodejs/",
